'''''Asparagus declinatus''''', common name '''bridal veil''', is a species of ''[[Asparagus (genus)|Asparagus]]'' plant. It is native to the [[Cape Provinces]], [[Madagascar]] and [[Namibia]] and has been introduced into Central America, [[South Australia]] and [[Western Australia]].<ref name="powo">{{cite taxon |powo |title=''Asparagus declinatus'' L. |id=531065-1 |access-date=2 March 2024}}</ref> It is a perennial vine. It is categorized as invasive in some areas.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://weeds.brisbane.qld.gov.au/weeds/bridal-veil|title=Bridal veil|website=Weed Identification – Brisbane City Council}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Bridal veil (''Asparagus declinatus'') Fact Sheet |url=https://cdn.environment.sa.gov.au/landscape/docs/hf/Bridal-veil-fact-sheet.pdf |access-date=2026-03-18 |website=Landscape South Australia Hills and Fleurieu}}</ref>

